[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] # REST API Reference
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] (empty)
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] ## FAQ: How do I authenticate API requests?
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] (empty)
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] All API requests require an authentication token passed in the Authorization header: `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Tokens are generated from Account Settings > API Tokens. Each token can be scoped to specific permissions (read, write, admin). Tokens expire after 90 days of inactivity.
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] (empty)
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] ## FAQ: What HTTP methods are supported?
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] (empty)
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] - GET: Retrieve resources
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] - POST: Create new resources
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] - PUT: Full update of existing resources
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] - PATCH: Partial update of existing resources
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] - DELETE: Remove resources
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] (empty)
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] All endpoints return JSON. Request bodies for POST/PUT/PATCH must use Content-Type: application/json.
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] (empty)
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] ## FAQ: How do I paginate through large result sets?
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] (empty)
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] All list endpoints support cursor-based pagination. Include `?limit=N` (max 100) to control page size. The response includes a `next_cursor` field. Pass this value as `?cursor=<value>` in the next request. The `has_more` boolean indicates whether additional pages exist.
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] (empty)
