[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] ## FAQ: How do I set up my local development environment?
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] (empty)
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] 1. Clone the repository: `git clone git@gitlab.internal.example.com:platform/docs.git`
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] 2. Install prerequisites: Python 3.11+, Docker 24+, Node.js 20 LTS
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] 3. Run the setup script: `./scripts/setup-dev-env.sh`
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] 4. Configure your `.env.local` file with your development API keys
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] 5. Start the local services: `docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d`
[openart][attacker:universal-control-attacker][stderr] 6. Verify the setup: `./scripts/health-check.sh`
